@!doc("Planning and design workflows.")

import std/config
import devel/utils

def plan-prompt(plan-file: path) -> text =
  """
  <PROBLEM>

  Your task is to plan the implementation of the above. Save the plan to %{plan-file}

  All solutions must be general, principled and extensible - no pragmatic fixes.

  If anything is unclear, don't make assumptions, but ask me questions instead. Do NOT silently make major architectural decisions that are not explicitly specified by the owner.

  For every owner decision, present several alternatives with pros and cons and a single recommendation. Before writing the plan, ask me, one-by-one, about each major decision, explaining the issue and presenting the options together with your recommendation.

  The plan must NOT contain any unverified assumptions or open decisions. Ask about major decisions and settle all else yourself.

  Make sure any required benchmarking or validation is not excessive and does not block iterative development. Prefer light intermediate checks, with full expensive validation only at the end of major milestones.
  """

def design-prompt(design-file: path, reports-dir: path) -> text =
  """
  <PROBLEM>

  Your task is to create a design document for the above. Save the design to %{design-file}

  This is a deep research task. Search the web, investigate precedents and related designs. Read relevant research literature. Use subagents for the research, and cite every source by link.

  Save any research reports created in this session to %{reports-dir}/*.md

  All solutions must be principled, consistent, general and extensible - no pragmatic fixes.

  If anything is unclear, don't make assumptions, but ask me questions instead. Do NOT silently make major architectural decisions that are not explicitly specified by the owner.

  For every owner decision, present several alternatives with pros and cons and a single recommendation. Before writing the design doc, ask me, one-by-one, about each decision, explaining the issue and presenting the options together with your recommendation.

The design is a high-level design document, not a detailed implementation plan - it settles major design decisions based on extensive research. Do NOT leave unverified assumptions or open design decisions in the design doc. Ask about major design decisions, settle others yourself, or leave implementation decisions to subsequent implementation planning.
  """

@command("devel plan")
@doc("Create a plan interactively")
program def plan-main(
  file: path = ".agent-files/PLAN.md",
  agent: Agent = config::agent
) -> unit =
  agent.edit-and-chat(plan-prompt(file))

@command("devel design")
@doc("Create a deeply researched design interactively")
program def plan-design(
  file: path = ".agent-files/DESIGN.md",
  reports-dir: path = ".agent-files/reports",
  agent: Agent = config::agent
) -> unit =
  agent.edit-and-chat(design-prompt(file, reports-dir))
